projection — Explains interface value projections and associated type projections.

Syntax:
  function label(user: User) -> string {
    return user.as<Named>.name
  }
  
  function head<S extends Stream>(stream: S) -> (S as Iterator).Item? {
    return stream.next()
  }
  
  type Parsed = (IntParser as Parser).Output

`value.as<Interface>` selects an interface view for member access. `T.Assoc`, `Self.Assoc`, and `(T as Interface).Assoc` project associated types in type positions; use the qualified `(T as Interface).Assoc` form when multiple required interfaces define the same associated type name. `Type.as<Interface>` is not type syntax.
